## Comparison Baselines (Wf-431 refactor — alignment 不是 reproduction)

**Principle** (per user directive 2026-10-01): **我们不需要 reproduce 别人的数字 — 我们需要 same dataset + same protocol + same metric 来 make results comparable.**

Selected baselines (Tier-1 direct comparison):

| # | Baseline | Dataset | Why selected |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Krasnov 2026** (*J. Med. Chem.*) | MetalCytoToxDB | 同领域 + 同任务 + 同 5-metal subset (Ru/Ir/Rh/Re/Os) |
| 2 | **Rusanov 2025** (ChemRxiv) | PlatinAI | 同金属 (Pt) + 同目标 (cisplatin-resistance) |
| 3 | **DrugOOD 2022** (ICLR) | DrugOOD | SBDD OOD generalization + iMoLD uses this dataset |

- Full per-paper detail + protocol alignment matrix: **`TODO/03_baselines/COMPARISON_BASELINES.md`**
- Quick reference table: **`TODO/03_baselines/PROTOCOL_ALIGNMENT_MATRIX.md`**
- Decision rationale: **`TODO/decisions.md` D-Wf-431**

The previous "reproduce baseline" approach (`TODO/archive/reproduce_baselines.md.archived_2026_10_01`) is DEPRECATED — we do NOT need to reproduce others' numbers; we just need comparable numbers.

